/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 284 0 R
/T (class InvalidRecord\(Exception\) is raised inside parse_line\(\) when a line does not have exactly 3 fields or when the status is not P or A. It is handled in summarise\(\) \(the loop which reads the file\), because only that function knows the line number and can decide to note the problem and go on with the next line. parse_line\(\) only reports the problem. Because it is separate from FileNotFoundError and the others, a damaged line \(a data problem\) is never confused with a missing file \(a system problem\). )
/E (class InvalidRecord\(Exception\) is raised inside parse_line\(\) when a line does not have exactly 3 fields or when the status is not P or A. It is handled in summarise\(\) \(the loop which reads the file\), because only that function knows the line number and can decide to note the problem and go on with the next line. parse_line\(\) only reports the problem. Because it is separate from FileNotFoundError and the others, a damaged line \(a data problem\) is never confused with a missing file \(a system problem\). )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
