/T (Open file when write\(\) fails: if write\(\) fails \(disk full, for example\) the exception leaves save_returns\(\) before log.close\(\) is reached. The file object stays open, its last data may not be flushed, and on Windows the file can stay locked. process\(\) only catches FileNotFoundError, so the error goes up and stops the program. )
/E (Open file when write\(\) fails: if write\(\) fails \(disk full, for example\) the exception leaves save_returns\(\) before log.close\(\) is reached. The file object stays open, its last data may not be flushed, and on Windows the file can stay locked. process\(\) only catches FileNotFoundError, so the error goes up and stops the program. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [11]
>>
