/T (I wrote a test which runs process\(\) for three days and prints the log after each day, then shows the raw content of the log, then tries a missing file, and finally simulates a failing write. The failing write is simulated with a small helper \(track.py\) which wraps open\(\) and raises OSError \("disk full"\) on the second write and remembers whether the file got closed. I used the helper because a real disk-full error is difficult to produce on purpose. )
/E (I wrote a test which runs process\(\) for three days and prints the log after each day, then shows the raw content of the log, then tries a missing file, and finally simulates a failing write. The failing write is simulated with a small helper \(track.py\) which wraps open\(\) and raises OSError \("disk full"\) on the second write and remembers whether the file got closed. I used the helper because a real disk-full error is difficult to produce on purpose. )
/Pg 34 0 R
