<<
/Title (Figure 61: List search compared with a set)
/Dest [71 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1912 0 R
/Next 1111 0 R
>>
endobj
1540 0 obj
<<
/Title (When n doubled \(4000 to 8000 and 8000 to 16000\) the list time grew about 4 times each time, which is the n squared behaviour, and the set time grew much more slowly \(between 1.5 and 3 times, and these times are so small that some of it is noise\). At n = 16000 the set was about 660 times faster. The extra memory of the set is small compared with this saving, so the set is the right choice for a registration desk which may have thousands of lines.)
/Dest [72 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1111 0 R
>>
