/Title (The alternative is to keep all the functions in one script. There is no import at all, so there is no import cost. For the package, the first import loads and compiles the files once and stores them in sys.modules, and every later import is only a dictionary lookup. I measured it.)
/Dest [57 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2790 0 R
/First 2815 0 R
/Last 2816 0 R
/Count -4
/Next 2803 0 R
>>
endobj
2803 0 obj
<<
/Title (The import cost is paid once and does notdepend on how much data the program processes, so itis O\(1\) with respect to the data. For anassignment sized program the cost is not noticeable, and the better structure is worth it.)
/Dest [58 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2790 0 R
/Prev 2802 0 R
>>
endobj
