2874 0 obj
<<
/Title (BothareO\(1\)perline, so O\(n\)forthe file, and both use O\(1\) extra space. When bad linesare rarethetryblockcosts almostnothing, because setting it up is cheap. When many lines are bad,raisingandcatching an exception for each one costs more than an if. So for data thatis almostcleanIprefer try/except,and for data that is full of mistakes the if checks are faster.For files,try/exceptalso avoids theproblem that a file can disappear between checking that it existsandopeningit.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2870 0 R
/Prev 2873 0 R
>>
endobj
